# A CLASS ASSERTION OVER AN ANONYMOUS CLASS EXPRESSION. `:a a [ ∃op.⊥ ]` is
# ClassAssertion(∃op.⊥, a): in v0, and INCONSISTENT, since ∃op.⊥ is empty.
# A decoder that only reads `rdf:type` with an IRI object files it as
# unrecognized: sound (the omission blocks COHERENT) but INCONCLUSIVE where
# the answer is known. Found by the W3C OWL 2 conformance test
# WebOnt-Restriction-001 (corpus/conformance.py); this is its shape.
# Expect: INCOHERENT (inconsistent), omitted 0, exit 1.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:op a owl:ObjectProperty .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual ,
     [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :op ; owl:someValuesFrom owl:Nothing ] .
